d-bbac-473c2a705ba0" :question/math-academy-id "q-82286" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|A|=(-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1=-\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|C|=4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2=-8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82286/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82286"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140046/selection/9a706cca3397926462882659e466a6cfa02e6978e78d1951ccab85cbb33685e2" :answer/id #uuid "517794bf-90c2-52a5-b8c5-803a3117a1d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140046/selection/ffe2658b61fb7d0dab3ff632e5bb0010b15c994dbe221a53ea11b11f42a36f3b" :answer/id #uuid "6d1691fe-902d-5280-9730-d67a6e4f69aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140046/selection/6f829e55765b65c548f374b89be5a8e1d2db51ecc82246a2b1b6e6f4fb2abf6b" :answer/id #uuid "cf2ce80f-425a-5f81-94c2-2b577e459a47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140046/selection/fa9e12c8b42568dd093650e15eee81422847cff71e4354f3171a249ad225e30d" :answer/id #uuid "c2df8e23-4502-5058-b902-4880ef765d2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140046/selection/f710292965833407c392cd64d43882cf3fc6c030eafd896396600d5acf92f9d9" :answer/id #uuid "e046d7a7-6981-5d4e-9895-430745cb90f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140046/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b2d02b9-5ebe-5fbd-aabd-ce7269173b9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140046/selection/9a706cca3397926462882659e466a6cfa02e6978e78d1951ccab85cbb33685e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-140046/selection/9a706cca3397926462882659e466a6cfa02e6978e78d1951ccab85cbb33685e2" "q-140046/selection/ffe2658b61fb7d0dab3ff632e5bb0010b15c994dbe221a53ea11b11f42a36f3b" "q-140046/selection/6f829e55765b65c548f374b89be5a8e1d2db51ecc82246a2b1b6e6f4fb2abf6b" "q-140046/selection/fa9e12c8b42568dd093650e15eee81422847cff71e4354f3171a249ad225e30d" "q-140046/selection/f710292965833407c392cd64d43882cf3fc6c030eafd896396600d5acf92f9d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140046" :question/id #uuid "3c1bd5a4-43fd-5d63-843c-209b976b49d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-140046" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The $A$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|A|=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1\\cdot 4=8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has identical columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(C)=5\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot (-10)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140046/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140046"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42959"] :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|B|=3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 5=-15\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42459"] :question/problem "Find $4det(A)+4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- For the matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-1\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4det(A)+4det(B)=4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 0=12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42882"] :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=1\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=12\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-140047/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "bfd98be9-b0cb-575b-94ab-5e3f5e8a6773" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140047/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "366280a1-aa2c-5458-9467-45985814efbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140047/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "dc38cc3f-2361-52ea-98d8-c55218b8d8a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140047/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a7